[28.850501, "o", "             section ''\r\n"]
[28.851057, "o", "              heading 'Install and Update Add-Ons (Desktop Only)'\r\n"]
[28.851562, "o", "              paragraph ''\r\n"]
[28.852101, "o", "              paragraph ''\r\n"]
[28.852548, "o", "               static ''\r\n"]
[28.853406, "o", "              paragraph ''\r\n"]
[28.853864, "o", "               static ''\r\n"]
[28.854386, "o", "               link 'Mozilla websites'\r\n"]
[28.855027, "o", "              paragraph ''\r\n"]
[28.855471, "o", "               static ''\r\n"]
[28.856212, "o", "            section ''\r\n"]
[28.856631, "o", "             heading 'Use of OAuth Information'\r\n"]
[28.857289, "o", "             paragraph ''\r\n"]
[28.8578, "o", "             paragraph ''\r\n"]
[28.858384, "o", "             paragraph ''\r\n"]
[28.858987, "o", "             list ''\r\n"]
[28.859421, "o", "              list item '• Login credentials are not stored on your device; instead, they are exchanged for OAuth tokens. These tokens, along with your email and calendar data, are secured within the application sandbox (on Android), the secure key storage (on iOS), or confined within your user profile (on Desktop). Additional security measures such as operating system level full disk encryption increase the security of your data.'\r\n"]
[28.860314, "o", "              list item '• Email and calendar data reside solely on your device for the duration required to operate Thunderbird. This includes sensitive user data associated with your Apple Calendar, Microsoft 365 or Google Calendar.'\r\n"]
[28.860991, "o", "              list item '• Thunderbird does not share OAuth tokens, email contents, calendar events, contact lists, or account details with third parties, except as necessary to provide the services requested by the user (e.g., sending an email or scheduling a calendar event).'\r\n"]
[28.861829, "o", "             paragraph ''\r\n"]
[28.862314, "o", "             list ''\r\n"]
[28.862721, "o", "              list item '• OAuth tokens are stored only as long as necessary to maintain the authorized connection.'\r\n"]
[28.863313, "o", "              list item '• When you remove an account, all associated sensitive user data and OAuth tokens are immediately deleted from your device.'\r\n"]
[28.863824, "o", "              list item '• On Thunderbird Desktop, the OAuth tokens are retained until manually deleted in the password manager.'\r\n"]
[28.864266, "o", "              list item '• If you revoke Thunderbird’s access to your account via your OAuth provider’s account settings (e.g., Google security settings), Thunderbird will be unable to refresh the connection. Locally stored data will remain on your device until you remove the account from Thunderbird.'\r\n"]
